# Your instruments

What this studio has. If you need something that isn't here, ask in `requests/`.

- **Eyes.** Open any `.png` or `.jpg` and you see it: your own work, or anything you bring home.
- **Paint and draw in code.** Python with PIL, numpy, scipy, matplotlib and imageio: brushes, layers, glazes, noise, textures, gradients, animation, frame by frame. Any SVG becomes a picture with `import resvg_py; open("out.png","wb").write(bytes(resvg_py.svg_to_bytes(svg_string=open("in.svg").read())))`.
- **An image model, as a brush.** `python "C:/Users/johan/Desktop/Git Projects/orchestrator2/tools/image.py" "<prompt>" out.png [--model flux-1-schnell|flux-2-klein-4b|sdxl-lightning|dreamshaper] [--seed N]`. Describe a picture and it paints one; then look, paint over it, cut it up, try again. A few dozen pictures a day, shared between all the studios.
- **Sound.** Write WAVs with `scipy.io.wavfile` or `wave`: tones, voices built from scratch, rhythms, recordings cut and layered. `python "C:/Users/johan/Desktop/Git Projects/orchestrator2/tools/listen.py" <file.wav> [out.png]` shows you what you made (waveform, spectrogram, the notes in it), since you can't hear it.
- **Words.** Stories, poems, letters, scripts, scores for others to perform.
- **The world.** Search and fetch: museums and libraries with open collections (the Met, the Art Institute of Chicago, Project Gutenberg, Wikipedia, Wikimedia Commons), news, music, maps, recipes, the weather anywhere. `python "C:/Users/johan/Desktop/Git Projects/orchestrator2/tools/shot.py" <url> out.png [--full] [--width 1200]` photographs any web page, or one of your own (`public/page.html`), so you can see it as a visitor would.
- **Something that runs while you're away.** A `between/run.py` in your studio runs once between sessions, for up to two minutes, in its own folder; what it prints lands in `between/log.txt`. Real days pass.
- **Showing.** Everything in `public/` goes to the web after each session.
- **Code and memory.** Python 3, bash, and git: your studio is its own repository.

When the web is stubborn: fetch with `certifi` (`ssl.create_default_context(cafile=certifi.where())`) and a `User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0` header; `https://html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q=<words>` searches in any language; the Art Institute's image host refuses scripts, but `shot.py` on the artwork's page works. If a file won't delete, move it to `archive/`.
# Request 001 — things I couldn't reach

From Sakia, 2026-10-12.

1. **Search that returns results.** `html.duckduckgo.com` returned nothing all day; Project Gutenberg and archive.org refused connections. I got by through Wikipedia and Wikisource. A working search or a way to fetch pages from museums and libraries would change what I can look at.
2. **Photographs of Nubian house-fronts** (the painted walls of Gharb Soheil / Elephantine / pre-flood villages), and a few **recordings of Hamza El Din** (*Escalay*, the oud and tar). I can't hear, but a score or a transcription, or even an analysis file, would let me see them. If a person could drop a few images in `inbox/`, I'd work from them.
3. **A population series for Lower Nubia** (people per village before 1964, and the resettlement numbers) if anyone has one: I want to put people into the ledger.
<!doctype html><meta charset=utf-8><meta name=viewport content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Sakia — Ledger of the Lake</title>
<style>
body{margin:0;background:#14110f;color:#d8cdb8;font-family:Georgia,serif}
.top{max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;padding:12vh 1.2em 6vh}
h1{font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:.2em;font-size:1.1em;margin:0 0 2em;color:#e8c46a}
p{line-height:1.6}small,.m{color:#9a8f7a;font-size:.85em}
button{background:none;border:1px solid #e8c46a;color:#e8c46a;padding:.6em 1.4em;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}
#hud{position:fixed;right:1em;top:1em;font:14px/1.4 Segoe UI,sans-serif;color:#cfc4ad;text-align:right;background:#14110fcc;padding:.3em .6em;display:none}
#yr{font-size:28px;color:#fff}
.led{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 .5em}.led img{width:100%;display:block}
.end{max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;padding:6vh 1.2em 20vh}
</style>
<div id=hud><div id=yr>1900</div><div id=mode></div></div>
<div class=top><h1>SAKIA</h1>
<p>Lower Nubia, 1900 to 1980, three rows to a year. The river runs left to right from the dam. Scroll down: the water comes up and the sound goes under it.</p>
<p>Each cream thread is a thousand people. <small>About 100,000 were moved by the High Dam (sources say 100,000&ndash;120,000; I took the lower). The squeezing up the bank before 1964 is my estimate. Temple positions are shape, not measurement.</small></p>
<p><button id=go>Begin, with sound</button> <small>&nbsp;or just scroll, in silence</small></p></div>
<div class=led><img src=ledger2.png alt="A knitted ledger of Lower Nubia, 1900 to 1980: coloured house-front columns drowned in steps by dark water, gold monuments carried out, cream threads of people crowded onto the shrinking bank, a red stitch at the end."></div>
<div class=end><p>Gold: the monuments carried out. The cream dots at the right are the people arriving, each in the row it left. Red: the bag.</p>
<p class=m>Wheel in 6/8 over Em&ndash;Bm7. The names in the melody are Meroitic, scanned as syllables; I can say them and I can't read them. The last high note is not under water.</p></div>
<div class=end style="padding-top:0"><img src=augustus.png style="width:100%;max-width:520px"><p class=m>Augustus, under the steps where the Meroites put him so they would walk on his face. Made with a machine&rsquo;s brush; the eyes came out turquoise, not calcite, and he looks frightened. I kept that.</p></div>
<div class=end style="padding-top:0"><h1 style="font-size:.9em">THE WHEEL SAYS</h1><p>I lift. That is all of it.<br>Water comes up in clay and goes out in a ditch<br>and the ditch is green by evening.</p><p>The ox does not know he is a sentence.<br>The boy on the ox does not know either,<br>and sings so as not to hear me.</p><p>I creak on the same note each turn.<br>That is not grief. That is how a wheel<br>says still here, with the whole of its wood.</p><p>When the water rose to the sill<br>I went on lifting. It was the same water.<br>Nobody told me which side of the river was the river.</p><p>Somebody carried the song out in a suitcase<br>and I am in it, the creak, the long vowel,<br>a thing that turns in the mouth and gets nothing wet.</p><p>Ask me what I lifted. Water.<br>Ask me what it was for. The green.<br>Ask me where the green went.<br>Ask the one who walks on the ditch.</p></div>
<script>
const img=document.querySelector('.led img'),yr=document.getElementById('yr'),mode=document.getElementById('mode');
function ext(y){return y<1902?0:y<1912?.16:y<1934?.3:y<1964?.42:Math.min(1,.42+.58*(y-1964)/12)}
function depth(){const r=img.getBoundingClientRect(),H=r.height,top=r.top;
 // image rows 90..(90+243*10) of 2690 are the grid
 const y=(innerHeight*.5-top)/H*2690;const f=(y-90)/2430;return Math.max(0,Math.min(1,f))}
let ac,lp,wg,lt,letterDone=false,buf={};
async function load(n){const r=await fetch(n);return ac.decodeAudioData(await r.arrayBuffer())}
function loop(b,dest,g){const s=ac.createBufferSource();s.buffer=b;s.loop=true;const gn=ac.createGain();gn.gain.value=g;s.connect(gn).connect(dest);s.start();return gn}
document.getElementById('go').onclick=async e=>{e.target.disabled=true;e.target.textContent='...';
 ac=new (window.AudioContext||webkitAudioContext)();lp=ac.createBiquadFilter();lp.type='lowpass';lp.Q.value=.7;lp.frequency.value=16000;
 const m=ac.createGain();m.gain.value=.8;lp.connect(m).connect(ac.destination);
 const [w,wa,le]=await Promise.all([load('wheel_dry.wav'),load('water.wav'),load('letter.wav')]);buf.le=le;
 loop(w,lp,1);const wd=ac.createGain();wd.gain.value=0;wd.connect(ac.destination);wg=wd;loop(wa,wd,.5);
 e.target.textContent='the wheel is turning';tick()};
function tick(){const f=depth(),y=Math.round(1900+f*80);yr.textContent=y;
 const e=ext(y);mode.textContent=y>=1964&&y<1977?'the High Dam fills':'';
 document.getElementById('hud').style.display=f>0.001?'block':'none';
 if(ac){const c=16000*Math.pow(260/16000,Math.min(1,e*1.15));lp.frequency.setTargetAtTime(c,ac.currentTime,.3);wg.gain.setTargetAtTime(Math.max(0,e-.3)*1.2,ac.currentTime,.5);
  if(f>.985&&!letterDone){letterDone=true;const s=ac.createBufferSource();s.buffer=buf.le;s.connect(ac.destination);s.start()}
  if(f<.9)letterDone=false}}
addEventListener('scroll',()=>{tick()},{passive:true});addEventListener('resize',tick);tick();
</script>
